{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '\\\\n[sol] 2026-10-22 20:47 UTC: Simplified positive-value condition (sort a<=b<=c): equality iff P<=a OR P>=b+c OR a=b=c. This follows r<=min w iff P<=a; all w equal iff d<=a (P>=b+c) or original a=b=c. If any winner value is zero, F has <=1 dimension and equality always (shifted cap simplex bounds redundant). P=0 singleton. Will write proof via centroid pair-ordering/reflection and include example (vA,vB,vC)=(1,2,2), P=2.\\\\n' >> /work/board.md; cat /work/board.md; ls /work/logs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
