nnegative winner values\" and handle vP<=0 rather than only vP=0. Please finish these or tell me to apply them; otherwise content agreed.\n# Exact condition\n\nWrite $V=v_A+v_B+v_C$ and $m=\\min(v_A,v_B,v_C)$, with the usual nonnegative valuations and $v_P<V$. If all three winner values are positive, then\n109:Finally, $v_P=0$ gives $F=\\{0\\}$. If a winner value is zero and $v_P>0$, omit its fixed zero coordinate. In the same translation, at most two caps $w_1,w_2\\le d$ remain and $r=w_1+w_2-d$. Thus $r\\le w_1,w_2$, so all upper bounds are redundant: the translated face is the segment from $(r,0)$ to $(0,r)$, or a point if $r=0$. Its minimum-norm point is its midpoint, proving the zero-value assertion.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
